dsmr-email-encabulator (1.0-18) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Style the generated HTML documentation site with a vendored, offline copy
    of Water.css (a minimal classless stylesheet, MIT-licensed): automatic
    light/dark, readable typography, and styled tables/code without an external
    CDN.  The export emits semantic header/main/footer wrappers and a plain
    table-of-contents (not a <nav>, which classless frameworks mis-style as a
    menu bar).  Subscript/superscript export is disabled so identifiers such as
    UPGRADE_LEGACY render verbatim.  Dropped the auto-generated sitemap.
  * Generalize the shipped documentation for public reuse: references to the
    maintainer's production hosts, domains, and addresses are replaced with
    neutral example.* equivalents throughout the topic manuals and common
    docs, so the manuals no longer describe one specific live deployment.
  * Drop an internal operations report that was specific to a single
    production host and not relevant to general use; it is removed from the
    package payload and from the documentation index.

